            {
                "entry_id": "4ae42f67-bc63-3860-9fa0-1d71153d2937",
                "word": "Chagall",
                "pos": "name",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6645e206-c825-372f-85d6-68db9020665f",
                        "entry_id": "4ae42f67-bc63-3860-9fa0-1d71153d2937",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A surname from French; (art) used specifically of Marc Chagall (1887–1985), a Russian-French artist of Belarusian Jewish origin, renown for his use of colors and as a pioneer of modernism, incorporating elements of symbolism, fauvism, and cubism."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "76763666-011e-46a9-9305-5b8a168f01d3",
                                "sense_id": "6645e206-c825-372f-85d6-68db9020665f",
                                "text": "“What's tha most monay for a paintin' eva?” ¶ She smiled. “Well, last month I sold a Braque for two million and a Chagall oil for four million. […]”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "20a593c3-0bd1-41fd-a123-f1ebf547160b",
                                "sense_id": "6645e206-c825-372f-85d6-68db9020665f",
                                "text": "Images of flying brides, goats, acrobats and musicians recur again and again in the work of Chagall, each time reworked through the colour spectrum in a world at once harmonious and spiritual."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "7606e6c8-0367-373f-8c1f-d6a21acc9824",
